{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Whom she bore to him in Paddan Aram.</b> But Binyamin was not born in Paddan Aram! Rather, this is what it says: whom she bore to him through the prayer that Rachel prayed <b>in Paddan Aram</b>, when she said, 'May YHWH add me another son,' and from this the verse reckons him as though he were born in Paddan Aram. Another interpretation: since the majority of them were born in Paddan Aram, it is as though all of them were born there — just as we find in the portion of Vayigash: those who came to Egypt were seventy, yet Yosef and his two sons and Yokheved were included in the count, because the verse follows the majority."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:26.934638078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}